meta {
  name: 61 Master Data Import Sync (E2E)
  seq: 61
}

docs {
  End-to-end cases for **POST /master-data/branch/import-from-tenant** (Tenant Master
  Data → Branch Master Data). Self-contained: creates its own tenant, branch and
  branch admin, then walks the sync through every case. Run it against a
  throwaway database — it creates data.

    bru run "61 Master Data Import Sync (E2E)" --env Local \
      --env-var baseUrl=http://localhost:3100/api/v1 --sandbox developer

  Cases (in order, each builds on the previous state):
    C01 import without an active branch → 400
    C02 first import clones every tenant test
    C03 re-import is idempotent (same branch ids)
    C04 tenant test deleted + re-created (same name, new code) → adopted by name,
        branch id kept (the Oct-2026 prod 500)
    C05 param code changed upstream → branch param id kept (matched by name)
    C06 tenant test renamed onto a deleted test's name → orphan removed first
    C07 two tenant tests swap names / codes → both branch rows keep their ids
    C08 hand-made branch test shares a tenant test's name → 409, nothing changed
    C09 hand-made test removed → import succeeds
    C10 hand-made branch test shares a tenant test's code → adopted (legacy)
    C11 panel membership remapped to branch test ids
    C12 concurrent imports serialise (no duplicates)
    C13 save state for the duplicate-link DB fixture (folder 62)
}
